  "answer": "To reduce the risk of users over-generalising from partial information and wrongly anticipating a robot's actions, it has been proposed to deploy coverage-augmented algorithmic teaching of robot objectives to end-users (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465). This is achieved through a mechanism of strategy coverage augmentation after posterior convergence: once the additional posterior gain falls below a certain threshold (ε), the system adds extra teaching examples by selecting one from each previously uncovered trajectory-strategy cluster (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465). This ensures that users are exposed to at least one example from every major strategy, helping them to accurately anticipate the autonomous vehicle's behavior even in novel situations (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465)."
